When a combination of arms $S_t$ is selected in round $t$, a random outcome $X_{i,T_{i,t}}$ is generated (independently) from underlying distribution $
u_i$ for each $i \in S_t$. However, these outcomes remain unobserved. Instead, for each $i \in S_t$, a \emph{filtered observation} $Y_{i,T_{i,t}}$ is drawn from a \emph{filtering distribution} $	ilde{
u}_{i,T_{i,t}}=	ilde{
u}_i(X_{i,T_{i,t}},S_t)$ conditioned on the random outcome from the underlying distribution and the combination of arms played.

